: "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Derek Schmidt (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Kansas' 2nd District carries a ten-point Republican lean, and incumbent Derek Schmidt enters November as the clear favorite over Democrat Don Coover and Libertarian John Hauer. Raters across the spectrum place the race between Likely R and Safe R, and prediction markets give Schmidt roughly a four-in-five chance of holding the seat.\n\nCoover has run a well-funded challenge, raising about $1.4 million to Schmidt's $1.8 million, and the only poll available, conducted for the DCCC, shows a three-point contest. A national environment favoring Democrats this year adds some uncertainty to the picture. Still, Schmidt's incumbency, his cash-on-hand advantage, and the district's underlying partisanship make an upset possible but unlikely, keeping the race in Likely R territory.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0506, "margin": -10.48}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0308, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0524, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0445, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0597, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0512, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0416, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0318, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0398, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0406, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0253, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0744, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0619, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0457, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0427, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0316, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.038, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0474, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0379, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", 